## Section1('16.8')
## Problem1('3')
## KEYWORDS(equilibrium, force, Hooke's, spring, energy, potential, Newton, law)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl',  'PGcourse.pl');


$mass = random(0.2,1,0.01);
$force = random(25,50,1);

$A1 = ($mass)*(9.8)/($force);
$A2 = ($mass)*(9.8)*($A1);

BEGIN_PGML

a) How much will a spring that has a force constant of [`[$force]`] [`\textrm{N/m}`] be stretched by an object with a mass of [`[$mass]`] [`\textrm{kg}`] when hung motionless from the spring?

    Spring is Stretched [_]{$A1} m

b) Calculate the decrease in gravitational potential energy of the [`[$mass]`]-[`\textrm{kg}`] object when it descends this distance.

    [_]{$A2} J

END_PGML
BEGIN_PGML_HINT
a) The hanging object will have extended the spring by its equilibrium distance (that is, it will hang motionless) when the object's weight and the spring force balance.

b) Take the equilibrium distance to be the level of zero gravitational potential energy.
END_PGML_HINT

ENDDOCUMENT();
